C2C(1)                        C2C Manual                        C2C(1)

NAME
    c2c — the Cache-to-Cache middleware console utility

SYNOPSIS
    c2c [-h] [--version] COMMAND [OPTION] [ARGUMENT] ...
    c2c-serve [--host HOST] [--port PORT] [--certfile FILE] [--keyfile FILE]
    c2c-mcp

DESCRIPTION
    C2C lets heterogeneous LLMs communicate through directly fused
    KV-Caches instead of text (Fu et al., Cache-to-Cache: Direct Semantic
    Communication Between Large Language Models, ICLR 2026,
    arXiv:2510.03215v2).

    C2C is middleware, not a harness. It never owns an agent loop, tool
    dispatch, or session management. The harness stays the master; C2C is
    the wire between models.

COMMANDS
    The set of recognised commands (there is deliberately NO run-agent):

    doctor
        Check the installation, check the engines, report the findings;
        exit status 1 with --strict when a check failed.

    eval
        Run the golden regression against the paper (Tables 1-15 as
        pytest cases). Options: --table N (repeatable), -k EXPR, -v.

    fuse
        Fuse two caches into one, print the FusionReport. Mandatory:
        --receiver ID --sharer ID. Options: --engine ENGINE, --prompt
        TEXT, --fraction F (0..1 or 0..100), --direction former|latter,
        --variant simple|c2c-c, --seed N, --report, --answer.

    man [TOPIC]
        Format the manual pages. Topics: c2c, commands, config, fuser,
        engines, zoo, serve, proxy, mcp, a2a. Without TOPIC, the overview.

    serve
        Start the OpenAI-compatible HTTPS front; see c2c-serve(1) for
        the whole option list (routes: /v1/chat/completions,
        /v1/completions, /v1/models, /healthz).

    train
        Fit the fuser on a dataset; the two LLMs stay frozen. Mandatory:
        --receiver ID --sharer ID --dataset FILE. Options: --engine
        ENGINE, --epochs N, --lr RATE, --total-steps N, --out FILE,
        --variant simple|c2c-c, --seed N, -v.

    zoo ACTION
        The zoo maintenance interface for trained fusers. Actions: list,
        publish, get, remove (options per action: --sharer ID --receiver
        ID --checkpoint FILE --name NAME).

EXIT STATUS
    0   success (and peace: the pager hung up, the pipe delivered all)
    1   the work went wrong: the models could not be built, the dataset was
        not found, the zoo has no such entry, the port refused to bind, a
        module of the ML backend is absent, or a check failed under --strict
    2   the command line was wrong: argparse usage errors, tables without
        kept numbers, the dev extra missing for the requested eval, or an
        HTTP transport launched off the loopback without a key
    130 died by ^C — 128 + SIGINT, as is the way of the shells

ENVIRONMENT
    C2C_SEED, C2C_DEVICE, C2C_ROOT, C2C_FUSER_VARIANT, C2C_FUSER_DROPOUT,
    C2C_GATE_TAU_MAX, C2C_GATE_TAU_MIN,
    C2C_ALIGN_LAYERS, C2C_LR, C2C_MACRO_BATCH, C2C_MAX_SEQ,
    C2C_TOTAL_STEPS, C2C_HOST, C2C_PORT, C2C_API_KEY, C2C_PRIVACY,
    NO_COLOR / FORCE_COLOR. Environment variables win over the
    configuration file; see c2c.config(5).

FILES
    $C2C_ROOT/config.json        JSON overlay (defaults: ~/.cache/c2c)
    $C2C_ROOT/zoo/<pair>/        local zoo of trained fuser weights

SEE ALSO
    c2c.config(5), c2c.fuser(5), c2c.zoo(5), c2c.engines(7),
    the paper arXiv:2510.03215v2, the code and the tests.

